    "broke-my-mug-not-my-song":{"search": "I can hear the birds chirping and the sun’s setting, but it’s bright. Squinting my eyes in the light. It’s a world full of people and sounds. My place in this is lost, never found, never settles down. I might be touching ground, have been flying with my life. Wonder if what I imagined will feel worth it when it’s right. Suppose I’ll still feel misery whether I stay close to ground, Or whether I lift off into galaxies unbound, and never come back down. And I don’t know if I’m healing, Or just learning how to float. I keep reaching for a feeling That I swear I used to know. Maybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud, Made to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds. Maybe I’ll find peace where the stars don’t make a sound, Or maybe I’ll lift off and never come back down. Never come back down. Never come back down. If I can’t find my place here, I’ll be somewhere I can’t be found. I can hear the world moving like it knows where it should go. Everybody’s got a rhythm, I’m just standing in the glow. Trying to look normal with a storm behind my eyes. Smiling at the sunset while I’m disappearing inside. And maybe I’m dramatic, maybe I just feel too much. Maybe I’m just tired from surviving without touch. Maybe all this distance is the price of staying proud. Maybe I’m already gone and just haven’t said it loud. And I don’t know if I’m breaking, Or becoming something new. I keep staring at the sky Like it might tell me what to do. Maybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud, Made to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds. Maybe I’ll find peace where the stars don’t make a sound, Or maybe I’ll lift off and never come back down. Never come back down. Never come back down. If I can’t find my place here, I’ll be somewhere I can’t be found. Close to ground, I feel the weight. Far from home, I feel the same. Call it freedom, call it fate. Either way, I carry pain. But there’s a light I haven’t reached. There’s a version I might meet. Maybe somewhere past this grief, There’s a life that feels like me. Maybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud, Made to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds. Maybe I’ll find peace where the stars don’t make a sound, Or maybe I’ll lift off and never come back down. Never come back down. Never come back down. If I can’t find my place here, I’ll be somewhere I can’t be found. I can hear the birds chirping and the sun’s setting, but it’s bright. Squinting my eyes in the light. It’s a world full of people and sounds. My place in this is lost, never found, never settles down. I woke up in a supermarket cathedral, Wearing a necktie made of caution tape. The moon was frying eggs on a car hood, And the sun had a raccoon for a face. I saw a preacher selling discount halos, Two for one beside the laundromat. A fish in a business suit kept screaming, “You can’t die yet, you still owe me tax.” Everything’s sticky, everything’s loud, There’s a clown in the mirror eating thunderclouds. I’d laugh if my teeth weren’t glued to the floor, Knocking on heaven through a bathroom door. Needing connection does not make you weak, It makes you human, tragically. A gorgeous disaster with coffee-stain wings, Dragging a throne through a yard sale of kings. Needing connection does not make you weak, It makes you human, unfortunately. A shopping cart chariot, flat tire dreams, Still somehow rolling through the gasoline rain. There’s a choir of pigeons in a casino, Singing hymns through a nicotine storm. A beauty queen vomits glitter in slow-mo, While Cupid gets arrested for fraud. The sky wears fishnets, the road smells jealous, There’s a black-tie funeral for dignity. A mime got rich selling invisible sandwiches, Now he owns half the city and three minor seas. Everything’s melting, everything bites, There’s a priest on a skateboard blessing fistfights. I’d pray if the ceiling would stop chewing gum, And the jukebox quit swallowing everyone. Needing connect", "snippet": "I can hear the birds chirping and the sun’s setting, but it’s bright.", "lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nI can hear the birds chirping and the sun’s setting, but it’s bright.\nSquinting my eyes in the light.\nIt’s a world full of people and sounds.\nMy place in this is lost, never found, never settles down.\n\nI might be touching ground, have been flying with my life.\nWonder if what I imagined will feel worth it when it’s right.\n\nSuppose I’ll still feel misery whether I stay close to ground,\nOr whether I lift off into galaxies unbound, and never come back down.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nAnd I don’t know if I’m healing,\nOr just learning how to float.\nI keep reaching for a feeling\nThat I swear I used to know.\n\n[Chorus]\nMaybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud,\nMade to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds.\nMaybe I’ll find peace where the stars don’t make a sound,\nOr maybe I’ll lift off and never come back down.\n\nNever come back down.\nNever come back down.\nIf I can’t find my place here,\nI’ll be somewhere I can’t be found.\n\n[Verse 2]\nI can hear the world moving like it knows where it should go.\nEverybody’s got a rhythm, I’m just standing in the glow.\nTrying to look normal with a storm behind my eyes.\nSmiling at the sunset while I’m disappearing inside.\n\nAnd maybe I’m dramatic, maybe I just feel too much.\nMaybe I’m just tired from surviving without touch.\nMaybe all this distance is the price of staying proud.\nMaybe I’m already gone and just haven’t said it loud.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nAnd I don’t know if I’m breaking,\nOr becoming something new.\nI keep staring at the sky\nLike it might tell me what to do.\n\n[Chorus]\nMaybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud,\nMade to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds.\nMaybe I’ll find peace where the stars don’t make a sound,\nOr maybe I’ll lift off and never come back down.\n\nNever come back down.\nNever come back down.\nIf I can’t find my place here,\nI’ll be somewhere I can’t be found.\n\n[Bridge]\nClose to ground, I feel the weight.\nFar from home, I feel the same.\nCall it freedom, call it fate.\nEither way, I carry pain.\n\nBut there’s a light I haven’t reached.\nThere’s a version I might meet.\nMaybe somewhere past this grief,\nThere’s a life that feels like me.\n\n[Final Chorus]\nMaybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud,\nMade to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds.\nMaybe I’ll find peace where the stars don’t make a sound,\nOr maybe I’ll lift off and never come back down.\n\nNever come back down.\nNever come back down.\nIf I can’t find my place here,\nI’ll be somewhere I can’t be found.\n\n[Outro]\nI can hear the birds chirping and the sun’s setting, but it’s bright.\nSquinting my eyes in the light.\nIt’s a world full of people and sounds.\nMy place in this is lost, never found, never settles down.", "sunoUrl": "https://suno.com/song/647f2c65-84d5-4c21-8d96-a9affb3a20f2", "clipIds": ["647f2c65-84d5-4c21-8d96-a9affb3a20f2", "21e0c5e2-888a-4d8e-a97a-4ff092b72819", "d8ab709d-ca66-4f34-bd79-fcdc288aa190", "17868bfa-0361-45b5-8e94-f222da19a3a0", "89a032ef-af2d-4de0-b3b2-52424cbe7aa3", "5e905328-7db3-4230-b17c-249f91872755"]},
