    "september-26th-heartbreak":{"search": "I was gonna write a love song But, before it finished, she was long gone Gave her in my heart, watched her captivate it Then her s seat's vacant, she escaped quick I don't know if I could go Back to who I was, she touched my soul, I felt my heart flutter and my brain fuzz I asked myself if I could be Respectful of her time I took time to think of her as family This was the girl who sat two seats in front of me She set my heart wild and free Oh, I'm wild and free Whether or not I mean to be Yeah, I'm wild and free But my heart's unhappy 'Cause I wanna love I wanna feel I wanna hurt It's a packaged deal I wanna hurt 'cause I wanna feel 'cause I wanna love I'm choosing love Heartbreak, heartbreak I never knew what it'd be like to lose you Heartbreak, heartbreak Now I see It's a painful reality Heartbreak, heartbreak Comes and goes It makes us grow Heartbreak, heartbreak You water me You are a planter I am your seed I am your seed Growing wild and free I was gonna write a sad song But then another girl came along And was helping me with heart break and anxiety She's an INFJ, such a gentle pea I've got a tattoo of the Grim Reaper Oh, I'm wild and free Oh, I'm wild and free So, I'm gonna love I'm gonna feel I'm gonna hurt It's a package deal I'm gonna hurt 'cause I'm gonna feel 'cause I'm gonna love", "snippet": "I was gonna write a love song", "lyrics": "[Intro]\n[acoustic piano playing rhythmic block chords]\n\n\nI was gonna write a love song\nBut, before it finished, she was long gone\nGave her in my heart, watched her captivate it\nThen her s seat's vacant, she escaped quick\nI don't know if I could go\nBack to who I was, she touched my soul, I felt my heart flutter and my brain fuzz\nI asked myself if I could be\nRespectful of her time \nI took time to think of her as family\nThis was the girl who sat two seats in front of me\nShe set my heart wild and free\nOh, I'm wild and free\nWhether or not I mean to be\nYeah, I'm wild and free\nBut my heart's unhappy\n'Cause I wanna love\nI wanna feel\nI wanna hurt\nIt's a packaged deal\nI wanna hurt 'cause I wanna feel 'cause I wanna love\n\nI'm choosing love\n\nHeartbreak, heartbreak\nI never knew \nwhat it'd be like to lose you\nHeartbreak, heartbreak\nNow I see\nIt's a painful reality\nHeartbreak, heartbreak\nComes and goes\nIt makes us grow\nHeartbreak, heartbreak\nYou water me\nYou are a planter\nI am your seed\nI am your seed\nGrowing wild and free\n\nI was gonna write a sad song\nBut then another girl came along\nAnd was helping me with heart break and anxiety\nShe's an INFJ, such a gentle pea\nI've got a tattoo of the Grim Reaper\nOh, I'm wild and free\nOh, I'm wild and free\nSo, I'm gonna love\nI'm gonna feel\nI'm gonna hurt\nIt's a package deal\nI'm gonna hurt 'cause I'm gonna feel 'cause I'm gonna love", "sunoUrl": "https://suno.com/song/dff144e6-7de2-4ca0-af21-897de1a4da8d", "clipIds": ["dff144e6-7de2-4ca0-af21-897de1a4da8d"]},
    "seven-days-locked":{"search": "Seven days locked where the lights don’t fade, Saw a man preaching fire like he carried the blade. He said angels were screaming through the hospital vents, I just smiled, played it cool, like I knew what he meant. If I lose my calm, then the room might break, But if I hold it steady, they’ll all feel safe. I’m the guard dog hiding in a paper gown, Growling quiet so no one drowns. I’ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd, Carrying the weight, never saying it out loud. If the voices come knocking, I’ll answer with grace, ’Cause somebody’s gotta hold the space. He said God was a pilot and the floor was the sky, Tried to jump off his bed just to learn how to fly. I caught his arm, laughed, said “save that trick, The food here’s bad but the gravity’s thick.” If I lose my calm, then the room might break, But if I hold it steady, they’ll all feel safe. I’m the guard dog hiding in a paper gown, Growling quiet so no one drowns. I’ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd, Carrying the weight, never saying it out loud. If the voices come knocking, I’ll answer with grace, ’Cause somebody’s gotta hold the space. Funny thing about hell—sometimes it’s just Tuesday, With bingo cards, pills, and the nurses on relay. But I learned in the storm when the world’s insane, You can still be the calm in somebody else’s brain. I’ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd, Carrying the weight, never saying it out loud. If the voices come knocking, I’ll answer with grace, ’Cause somebody’s gotta hold the space. Yeah—somebody’s gotta hold the space.", "snippet": "Seven days locked where the lights don’t fade,", "lyrics": "[Intro]\n[Genre: Alternative Rock]\n[Mood: Dark, Defiant, Reflective]\n[Tempo: Mid]\n[Energy: High]\n[Texture: Gritty]\n[Instrument: Electric Guitar (Distorted)]\n[Instrument: Synth (Atmospheric)]\n[Instrument: Drums (Punchy)]\n[Vocal Tone: Raw]\n[Vocal Effect: Reverb]\n[Vocalist: Male]\n[Harmony: Yes]\n\n[Verse 1]\nSeven days locked where the lights don’t fade,  \nSaw a man preaching fire like he carried the blade.  \nHe said angels were screaming through the hospital vents,  \nI just smiled, played it cool, like I knew what he meant.  \n\n[Pre-Chorus]  \nIf I lose my calm, then the room might break,  \nBut if I hold it steady, they’ll all feel safe.  \nI’m the guard dog hiding in a paper gown,  \nGrowling quiet so no one drowns.  \n\n[Chorus]  \nI’ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd,  \nCarrying the weight, never saying it out loud.  \nIf the voices come knocking, I’ll answer with grace,  \n’Cause somebody’s gotta hold the space.  \n\n[Verse 2]  \nHe said God was a pilot and the floor was the sky,  \nTried to jump off his bed just to learn how to fly.  \nI caught his arm, laughed, said “save that trick,  \nThe food here’s bad but the gravity’s thick.”  \n\n[Pre-Chorus]  \nIf I lose my calm, then the room might break,  \nBut if I hold it steady, they’ll all feel safe.  \nI’m the guard dog hiding in a paper gown,  \nGrowling quiet so no one drowns.  \n\n[Chorus]  \nI’ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd,  \nCarrying the weight, never saying it out loud.  \nIf the voices come knocking, I’ll answer with grace,  \n’Cause somebody’s gotta hold the space.  \n\n[Bridge]  \nFunny thing about hell—sometimes it’s just Tuesday,  \nWith bingo cards, pills, and the nurses on relay.  \nBut I learned in the storm when the world’s insane,  \nYou can still be the calm in somebody else’s brain.  \n\n[Final Chorus / Outro]  \nI’ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd,  \nCarrying the weight, never saying it out loud.  \nIf the voices come knocking, I’ll answer with grace,  \n’Cause somebody’s gotta hold the space.  \nYeah—somebody’s gotta hold the space.", "sunoUrl": "https://suno.com/song/3a9418e6-b884-413e-9135-d904e8bfde29", "clipIds": ["3a9418e6-b884-413e-9135-d904e8bfde29", "278dbbac-3ada-456e-a44c-92eb3378be05", "509147ff-abdc-445c-a475-6548fa10cde3"]},
